Preserve causal order and distinguish clock rates from received frequencies (@physics-spacetime-causality: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Connect-relativistic-momentum-energy-and-electromagnetic-frame-changes.lingua#r_00AA5B239C317ABD18D2FE89BC") { r_00F4F31E0DC57AC39F51E3B5DA
For a nonzero future causal displacement, ΔT>0 and |Δx|≤ΔT. Under an allowed boost, ΔT′=γ(ΔT−βΔx)≥γΔT(1−|β|)>0. A causal influence permitted by this model therefore cannot have its event order reversed by changing inertial frame. A spacelike pair can: (ΔT,Δx)=(1,2), β=3/5 gives (−1/4,7/4). Its interval is −3 in both frames. No rest-frame clock can travel between those events at a permitted speed; an ordering convention is not a faster-than-light signal.

Differentiate the boost along a one-dimensional path. For w=u/c, obtain w′=(w−β)/(1−βw). If |w|≤1 the denominator is positive. The identities 1−w′=(1−w)(1+β)/(1−βw) and 1+w′=(1+w)(1−β)/(1−βw) show causal speeds remain causal. Light retains w′=±1. If w=β the particle is stationary in S′. This formula compares coordinate velocities; it is not obtained by subtracting speeds of received images.

For a clock source receding from a stationary receiver in flat spacetime at β>0, successive emissions separated by proper time Δτ have lab emission separation γΔτ. During that interval the source travels βcγΔτ farther away, so the arrival interval is γ(1+β)Δτ. Hence received frequency divided by rest emission frequency is 1/[γ(1+β)]=√[(1−β)/(1+β)]. At β=3/5 the ratio is 1/2, whereas the coordinate clock-rate factor 1/γ is 4/5. The extra difference is propagation, not another change in the source clock. Reversing recession to approach reverses the appropriate factor.

In three dimensions transverse motion and changing direction require the relevant emission and reception geometry. In a medium, signal speed and dispersion introduce additional premises; the vacuum c postulate does not claim every pulse or material disturbance travels at c. Later astronomy must distinguish a spectral shift, peculiar motion, gravitational comparison and cosmic expansion before inferring a distance or velocity.

**Work:** derive the two identities preserving |w′|≤1, verify the numerical spacelike reversal, and calculate the received interval for the approaching counterpart. Explain why synchronizing clocks, comparing proper times and reading a spectrum are three related but different measurement problems. Use [Dynamics and Relativity by David Tong](../sources/Dynamics-and-Relativity-by-David-Tong.lingua#r_007464FDC6A818524F8C87C426) 7.2.2 and 7.2.5 for the causal and velocity argument; the received-pulse calculation here is an original explicit model.

